{"cluster_id": "C-3115", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B023-040"], "canonical_claim": "`MergeTreeData` part loading enumerates through `iterateDirectory`; a benign-absent result on a not-live disk can silently attach an empty table over intact data.", "issue_ids": ["C10"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-disk-lifecycle-problem-and-constraints.md#hard-constraints"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3116", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B026-038"], "canonical_claim": "A non-claiming reader has exactly one identified wrong-answer class: a superseded GC generation can disappear mid-scan, causing `openSourceEdgeRun` to throw `CORRUPTED_DATA` on a healthy pool; this is independent of mount ownership.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-25-cas-tool-read-without-ownership-design.md#safety-enumeration"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3117", "topic": "recover-and-mint read paths", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B028-064", "B031-043"], "canonical_claim": "`ensureRefTableRecovered` and `resolveNamespaceLife` can mint a `Live` catalog entry and durable `_ckpt` from a read path, so `existsFile` on a never-born namespace can perform durable writes. Additionally, `existsFile` on a never-born namespace can mint a catalog entry and publish `_ckpt` from a read path, multiplying writes to the pool-wide catalog; `dropNamespace`, `listRefs`, and `resolveRef` were also identified as recover-and-mint paths.", "issue_ids": ["R12"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-07-28-ref-rework-adjacent-findings.md#r12-read-births-namespace", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-31-stage-b-strategic-review-fable.md#premise-hotspot"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3118", "topic": "cancelled S3 read retry", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B032-076", "B051-026"], "canonical_claim": "The B117 fix stops `ReadBufferFromS3`'s outer retry loop after `KILL QUERY` by checking `CurrentThread::get().isQueryCanceled()`. Additionally, The outer retry loop in `ReadBufferFromS3::processException` could continue retrying transient errors after `KILL QUERY` even though the SDK retry strategy stopped on query cancellation.", "issue_ids": ["B117"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/upstream.md#L192-L203", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-cas-carve-script.md#L251-L257"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3119", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B033-082", "B044-005"], "canonical_claim": "`CasObjectStorageBackend::get` and `getStream` can return bytes from one object version with the size and identity token obtained by an earlier `HEAD` from another version.; `readManifest` caches bytes fetched at GET token `Tg` under the preceding HEAD token `Th`, rather than under the token of the object whose bytes were decoded.", "issue_ids": ["R2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/20260717_codex_review.md#high-severity", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L125-L136"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3120", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B034-040"], "canonical_claim": "Concurrent readers and writers of the same `detached/<part>` ref on local storage can observe a half-written object; S3 does not have this torn-read class because PUT completion is atomic.", "issue_ids": ["B66a"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/BACKLOG.md#local-backend"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3121", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B034-127"], "canonical_claim": "`Store::resolveRef` hardcodes `.manifest_size = 0`, causing `PartFolderView::weight()` to undercount the manifest body because its weight is `bytes + manifest_size`.", "issue_ids": ["B10"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/BACKLOG.md#read-write"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3122", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B039-140", "B039-141", "B041-110"], "canonical_claim": "`PartPathParser` duplicates the `store/<uuid[:3]>/<uuid>` fanout, detached and shadow names, mutable per-part file names, and part-name grammar instead of deriving them from canonical ClickHouse sources; its grammar misses the `patch-` prefix and format-version awareness.; The path parser must recognize Atomic and non-Atomic layouts, temporary part prefixes, detached, projections, FREEZE shadow paths, table-level files, and generic mountpoint files.; The consistency review recommends at minimum tying CAS UUID fanout and part-name parsing to canonical rules, while using a low-level shared header for constants to avoid inverting the `Disks` dependency direction.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["cas_disks_consistency_review.md#f7--partpathparser-duplicates-canonical-path-constants-and-part-name-grammar", "docs/superpowers/cas/datapartstorage-content-addressed-design-concern.md#L50-L74"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3123", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B041-111"], "canonical_claim": "A non-Atomic table named detached cannot always be distinguished from the reserved detached-parts directory when only the path string remains.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/datapartstorage-content-addressed-design-concern.md#L64-L74"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3124", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B044-004"], "canonical_claim": "The committed read pipeline discards the resolved manifest and ref after planning a deferred blob GET, so dropping the ref and completing GC can make the later GET fail with `FILE_DOESNT_EXIST` during a long read.", "issue_ids": ["R1", "X1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L88-L124"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3125", "topic": "CAS path re-parsing overhead", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-033", "B013-025", "B013-027"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS read path re-parses the full part path on every IMetadataStorage call (existsFile/getFileSize/getStorageObjects/... each independently run parsePartFilePath plus route with ~10-15 small allocations), versus 1-2 allocations for non-CAS metadata backends; getView's cache-hit path additionally takes the per-table state_mutex and per-disk explain_mutex (a test/log-only decision journal) on every file-open plus two cacheKey() heap allocations, causing real serialization on wide-table/high-concurrency CAS SELECTs. Proposed fix: resolve the route once per file-open (memoize per raw path) and make the explain journal opt-in behind a setting, disabled by default. Additionally, The CAS read path repeatedly parses the same raw part path for `existsFile`, `getFileSize`, `getStorageObjects`, and related metadata calls, causing repeated allocations per logical file-open.; The `getView` cache-hit path currently takes a per-disk `explain_mutex` and materializes `cacheKey()` repeatedly solely for a test/log-only decision journal.", "issue_ids": ["U#9"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/review1.md#major-issues", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup.md#L2346-L2505", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup.md#L2506-L2711", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup-design.md#L114-L119", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup-design.md#L121-L126"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3126", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-182"], "canonical_claim": "A coalesced shard read (single-flight read coalescing) has no deadline (F-N1): if the leader's GET hangs, all coalesced follower readers block indefinitely (a reader convoy) \u2014 a real liveness finding distinct from any correctness issue.", "issue_ids": ["F-N1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L738-L739"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3127", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-227"], "canonical_claim": "`DataPartStorageOnDiskFull::prepareRead` captures a raw `transaction.get()` pointer into a lambda, relying only on a prose comment asserting synchronous consumption \"on this branch\"; a future cache or async read stage could silently turn this into a dangling capture.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/05-integration.md#9-historical-smells"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3128", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B001-011", "B008-017"], "canonical_claim": "A live ref resolving to an absent manifest or blob raises FILE_DOESNT_EXIST rather than producing a silent empty read.; Phase 1 changes `resolveRouted` to return an immutable `PartFolderView`, returning `nullptr` for an absent ref and surfacing missing or corrupt live manifests as exceptions rather than substituting a result.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-phase1.md#task-6", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/00-REPORT.md#L322-L330"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3129", "topic": "single-flight part-folder views", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B001-062", "B008-043", "B008-073"], "canonical_claim": "CachedPartFolderAccess is a bounded validate-on-hit cache of immutable PartFolderView snapshots and uses single-flight cold builds. Additionally, The single-flight map coalesces concurrent cold `CachedForLoad` builds per `PartRefKey` through a shared future; its mutex is not held across ref resolution, manifest reads, or decoding, and leader failures propagate to followers. Additionally, Concurrent view construction for one `PartRefKey` shares one `readManifestShared` through `std::shared_future`; the cache mutex is never held across resolution, manifest read, or decode, and a leader exception reaches followers.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-phase4.md#task-2", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/01-frontend.md#L37-L50", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-design.md#single-flight"]}

